Note helper made by Jonathan Bitner 2026

1--Note for adding or changing drugs in drugDatabase --
2--Note for adding or changing variables
3--Note for adding animated text (fade-in, pause, fade-out) triggered by a button
4--Variable name and description
5--Adding a theme


1--Note for adding or changing drugs in drugDatabase --
    1- Add in alphabetical order, capitalization does not matter.
    2- Currently brand and generic names are set up individually
    3- Active elements are 'drug', 'quantity', 'diagnosis', and 'formulary'
        Only need to add formulary: false for non-formulary products.
        May possibly use other fields later, such as 'product', 'altQuantity' and 'altDiagnosis', but currently have no use.
    4- otherwise just copy and paste, add the new drug you want. 

2--Note for adding or changing variables --
    1- Define variable in the HTML document, such as a new question for member name.
    2- For checkboxes, decide what you would like it to say when the box is checked/not checked
        Add respective information to checkboxData[]    
            For example, if 'type' is not selected, the default response is '75-Standard PA'
            If 'type' is selected, it will be either '75+76' or '70'
    3- For inputs whose values change depending on value, i.e. require function/if statements, 
        Call function within buildNote() with the others.
        Define function below buildNote().
        For example, if 'information' is blank, change value to 'No previous authorizations.'
    3- Add to the list for the respective get___() function.
    4- Add to answer[].
    5- Add to buildNote().
    6- Add to variable list in readme below

3--Note for adding animated text (fade-in, pause, fade-out) --
    - Add a span where you would like the text to appear/disappear
        - Add descriptive ID
        - class='hideStart"
    - Call animateText('spanID') 

4--Variable name and description --
    age	        Text        Member's age | 59 years
    chart	    Checkbox    Are there items in Chart View? | No items in Chart View
    clinical	Textarea    Clinical review based on chart notes
    comment     Select      Select which comment to add to tech note | Please approve as, Reviewed as
    conclusion	Textarea    Recommendation/Rationale
    diagnosis	Text        Diagnosis provided | T2DM
    drug	    Text        Drug name | Mounjaro
    expedited   Checkbox    Expedited in rxcrt channel | Expedited
    falseQL	    Checkbox    If reject 76, is it a true QL reject? | Not a true QL request
    gender	    Checkbox    Member's gender | fe/male
    claims	    Textarea    Claims history per Snapshot and/or COS | Snapshot shows paid claims for...
    information	Textarea    Details related to approvals
    member	    Text        Date/range member joined | Member since 1-2026
    properQuantityText      The quantity the provider intended to submit | Instead of #4/28, should be #2/28.
    qset	    Checkbox    Result of provider's response to the q-set | Approval, Denial
    quantity	Text        Quantity and day supply | #2/28 days
    records	    Checkbox    Did provider submit documents with request? | Records submitted with request
    reject	    Radio       Reject code | 75, 75+76, 76
    snapshot	Checkbox    Are there results in Snapshot? | Paid claims, no paid claims
    source	    Select      Source of PA request | Fax, Phone, Web, Other
    state	    Select      Member's state | FL
    type	    Checkbox    Case review type | Initial/primary, Reauthorization, Reopening
    urgent	    Checkbox    Provider requested expedited review | Urgent


5-- Adding a theme
    1- Add option to theme selector in html document
    1.a or add to themeBook, hopefully someday I will create a function to automatically add all of the theme as options in the selector.
    2- Add in themes.css by category by alphabet, description below
        --main-background:      Webpage background.
        --header-background:    Top of the note, e.g. Note helper, Saved Note #1
        --footer-background:    Bottom of the note, where the buttons are
        --body-primary-color:   Saved notes (not note builder)
        --body-secondary-color: Bar that crosses middle of note builder, commonly use low-alpha white (#ffffff40)
        --body-border-color:    Border for notes.
        --body-gradient:        Add multiple colors for gradient effect, one color for solid.

        /* Text */
        --heading-text:         Top of the note, e.g. Note helper, Saved Note #1
        --animated-text:        Animated text, such as appears after button clicked.
        --body-text:            Note builder top/bottom sections, associated with --body-gradient
        --body-secondary-text:  Note builder middle section, associated with --body-secondary-color
        --input-text:           Text in bubbles i.e. text and textarea
        --input-text-focus:     " when focus.
        --placeholder-text:     Placeholder text in bubbles i.e. text and textarea
        --hyperlink-static:     I really ignore these colors, I just have them match the buttons somehow.
        --hyperlink-hover: 
        --hyperlink-active: 
        --hyperling-visited: 
        
        /* Buttons */
        --button-background:    self-explanatory.
        --button-hover: 
        --button-active:
        --button-text:

        /* Input */
        --input-background:         Background for bubbles, i.e. text and textarea
        --input-background-focus:   text/area when clicked
        --input-accent-color:       Checkbox color when checked
        --input-border:             text/area border
        --input-border-focus:       text/area border when clicked